# CLAUDE.md

This file provides guidance to Claude Code (claude.ai/code) when working with code in this repository.


## IMPORTANT THINGS TO REMEMBER / DO 

When editing a file - always write the code first then do the imports

Try not to use "any" as types - make sure we are using correct type hinting when available.

## Commands

### Development
- `npm run dev` - Start development server on http://localhost:1420
- `npm run build` - Production build
- `npm run preview` - Preview production build on http://localhost:4173

### Code Quality
- `npm run lint` - Format and lint code using Biome (formats and fixes automatically)

### Testing
- `npm run test:unit` - Run unit tests with Vitest
- `bunx vitest run tests/unit/path/to/specific.test.tsx` - Run specific unit test
- `npm run test:unit --coverage` - Generate test coverage report
- `npm run test:integration` - Run integration tests
- `npm run test:e2e` - Run end-to-end tests with Playwright

### Other Commands
- `npm run update-icons` - Update Icon types after adding new icons to sprite.svg

## Architecture Overview

This is OpenBB Workspace, a financial data visualization web application built with React, TypeScript, and Vite. It features a dashboard-based interface where users can create widgets to display financial data, charts, and AI-powered insights.

### Core Technologies
- **React 18** with TypeScript for the UI layer
- **Vite** as build tool and development server
- **Zustand** for state management (global app state)  
- **Tailwind CSS** with custom design system components
- **Radix UI** for accessible UI primitives
- **TanStack Query** for data fetching and caching
- **React Router** for navigation
- **AG Grid** and **AG Charts** for data tables and visualizations
- **Plotly.js** and **Highcharts** for advanced charting
- **TradingView** charting library integration
- **Biome** for code formatting and linting
- **Vitest** for unit testing, **Playwright** for E2E testing

### Key Directories

#### `/src/components/`
- **AI/** - Copilot chat interface and AI-powered features
- **Widgets/** - Financial data widgets (charts, tables, economy data, equity analysis)
- **DataConnectors/** - Data source management and connection interfaces
- **LayoutAuth/** - Main authenticated app layout, sidebars, search
- **General/** - Shared UI components (tables, modals, forms)
- **ds/** - Design system components (atoms, dialogs, forms)

#### `/src/lib/`
- **state/** - Zustand stores for global state management
  - `app.ts` - Main application state (dashboards, widgets, layouts)
  - `auth.ts` - Authentication state
  - `copilot.ts` - AI chat state
  - `theme.ts` - Theme and appearance settings
- **api/** - API client functions and data fetching
- **utils/** - Utility functions for widgets, data processing, etc.

#### `/src/routes/`
Page components organized by route (login, dashboard, settings, etc.)

### State Management Pattern
Uses Zustand with subscribeWithSelector middleware. State is organized into domain-specific stores:
- App state handles dashboard layouts, widget management, and grid positioning
- Auth state manages user authentication and permissions  
- Copilot state manages AI chat sessions and context
- Each store uses TypeScript interfaces and includes both state and actions

### Widget System
The application centers around a flexible widget system:
- Widgets are React components that display financial data
- Support for various data sources (financial APIs, user uploads, SQL databases)
- Grid-based layout system using react-grid-layout
- Widgets can be parameterized, grouped, and share ticker symbols
- Export capabilities to Excel, PDF, and images

### Styling Approach
- Utility-first Tailwind CSS with custom design tokens
- CSS custom properties for theming (light/dark mode)
- Component-level styling using Tailwind classes
- Radix UI for accessibility and behavior
- Custom animations and micro-interactions

### Testing Strategy
- Unit tests in `/tests/unit/` mirror `/src/` structure
- Use React Testing Library for component testing
- E2E tests with Playwright for critical user flows
- Test files named with `.test.tsx` extension
- Use `data-testid` attributes for test element selection

### Icon Management
Icons are managed through an SVG sprite system:
1. Add SVG to `/public/assets/icons/sprite.svg`
2. Run `npm run update-icons` to regenerate TypeScript types
3. Use `<Icon id="icon-name" />` component

### Development Notes
- Uses path alias `~` for `/src` directory
- TradingView widgets require special handling for classname updates
- Custom classes prefixed with `_` (e.g., `_copy-chart-data-button`) are used for testing selectors
- Mobile-first responsive design approach
- PWA-enabled with service worker support

### Critical Type Definition Files
  When adding new features, always check and update these type definition files:

#### `/src/lib/types/app.ts`

-Contains Zod schemas for runtime validation
-Defines core data types: `TickerSchema`, `ParamDefSchema`, `WidgetSchemaBase`
-Widget visualization types in `WidgetVizTypes` array
-Chart types and table column definitions
**Must be updated when**: Adding new widget types, param types, or chart types